1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,674
Meet Rika: an AI agent that turns a pile of

2
00:00:03,674 --> 00:00:06,925
receipts into a submission-ready expense claim.

3
00:00:09,233 --> 00:00:13,788
Filing expenses is still painful. People type every bill in by hand,

4
00:00:13,788 --> 00:00:18,275
look up policy limits, and claims bounce back for a missing detail,

5
00:00:18,275 --> 00:00:21,758
a duplicate, or an item that was never reimbursable.

6
00:00:22,208 --> 00:00:26,204
And in India, many bills are printed in regional languages,

7
00:00:26,204 --> 00:00:27,558
or even handwritten.

8
00:00:29,667 --> 00:00:31,728
Rika does that work instead.

9
00:00:31,728 --> 00:00:35,630
An Angular app talks to a FastAPI back end over REST,

10
00:00:35,630 --> 00:00:37,692
and live server-sent events.

11
00:00:38,142 --> 00:00:41,126
A vision language model reads each document,

12
00:00:41,126 --> 00:00:45,265
deterministic checks verify the reading, and a policy engine,

13
00:00:45,265 --> 00:00:50,217
a duplicate detector and a question engine get the claim ready to submit.

14
00:00:52,638 --> 00:00:54,176
Let's sign in as Aarav,

15
00:00:54,176 --> 00:00:57,788
an engineer just back from a client trip to Bengaluru.

16
00:00:58,139 --> 00:01:02,215
His dashboard shows drafts in progress, money on its way,

17
00:01:02,215 --> 00:01:03,789
and spend by category.

18
00:01:05,002 --> 00:01:08,552
He starts a new claim, and Rika greets him in the chat.

19
00:01:08,902 --> 00:01:13,253
He drops in all seven files at once: a flight, a hotel invoice,

20
00:01:13,253 --> 00:01:18,502
two cab receipts, a team dinner, a coffee, and a phone photo of a café bill.

21
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:23,415
Each receipt now runs through a live pipeline: reading,

22
00:01:23,415 --> 00:01:28,617
extraction by a vision language model, a double-check pass, categorisation,

23
00:01:28,617 --> 00:01:31,600
policy validation, and duplicate detection.

24
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:36,034
This is Google's Gemma 3, a four-billion-parameter model,

25
00:01:36,034 --> 00:01:40,464
running locally through Ollama, so no document leaves the laptop.

26
00:01:40,464 --> 00:01:45,575
The same pipeline can switch to Claude, or to a fully offline rules engine.

27
00:01:46,795 --> 00:01:51,595
A few minutes later, everything is read, and organised by category.

28
00:01:51,796 --> 00:01:54,621
Rika capped the hotel at the lodging limit,

29
00:01:55,121 --> 00:01:59,471
deducted the craft beer from the dinner bill as non-reimbursable,

30
00:01:59,973 --> 00:02:03,048
flagged the second Uber receipt as a duplicate,

31
00:02:03,549 --> 00:02:06,524
and read the photographed café bill correctly.

32
00:02:07,130 --> 00:02:11,054
It also titled the claim, and wrote the remarks for the approver,

33
00:02:11,054 --> 00:02:12,805
from the receipts themselves.

34
00:02:13,405 --> 00:02:18,255
Instead of a long form, Rika asks only what it can't work out by itself.

35
00:02:18,455 --> 00:02:21,380
A one-line justification for the hotel,

36
00:02:23,073 --> 00:02:25,398
and whether to drop the duplicate.

37
00:02:25,699 --> 00:02:27,983
Every answer re-runs all the checks,

38
00:02:27,983 --> 00:02:30,774
and readiness climbs to one hundred percent.

39
00:02:31,370 --> 00:02:36,020
Aarav can also just ask. Rika answers from the live claim data.

40
00:02:43,869 --> 00:02:48,519
He reviews the summary, including the policy adjustments, and submits.

41
00:02:51,413 --> 00:02:54,712
The mock finance system issues a reference number,

42
00:02:54,712 --> 00:02:57,088
and routes the claim to his manager.

43
00:02:57,713 --> 00:03:01,893
Now Meera, his manager, signs in. A notification is waiting,

44
00:03:01,893 --> 00:03:04,888
and her approval queue shows the new claim.

45
00:03:08,636 --> 00:03:12,336
Every receipt, flag and attachment is in one place.

46
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:17,010
She adds a comment, and approves.

47
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:24,395
Back on Aarav's side, live notifications track every step.

48
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:29,888
Moments later, finance pays out the claim,

49
00:03:29,888 --> 00:03:32,920
and the timeline keeps a complete audit trail.

50
00:03:36,077 --> 00:03:40,120
The AI engine can be switched at runtime between Ollama, Claude,

51
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:43,152
and the offline engine, with live health checks.

52
00:03:43,664 --> 00:03:48,714
Categories, limits and rules all live in configuration, not in code.

53
00:03:50,533 --> 00:03:53,565
Under the hood: self-verifying extraction,

54
00:03:53,565 --> 00:03:58,402
a deterministic policy engine so the model never decides the money,

55
00:03:58,402 --> 00:04:00,857
duplicate detection across claims,

56
00:04:00,857 --> 00:04:04,033
and automatic fallback between AI providers.

57
00:04:04,483 --> 00:04:08,703
And all of it is covered by a comprehensive suite of unit tests,

58
00:04:08,703 --> 00:04:11,208
across the back end and the front end.

59
00:04:13,733 --> 00:04:17,833
Rika. Receipts in, reimbursement out. Thanks for watching!
